#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_ordered

#% text
# `is_ordered(xs)` tests whether the elements of `xs` are in canonical order; `is_ordered(xs, p)` whether `p(a, b)` holds for every pair of neighbours.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Equal neighbours count as ordered.

#% item
# Defined in the prelude through `ordered`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_ordered([1, 4, 2])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_ordered(["cat", "catfish", "fish"])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_ordered([1, 2, 2, 4])
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
is_ordered([4, 3, 2, 1], greater)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_ordered([4, 3, 3, 1], greater)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_ordered([4, 3, 3, 1], greater_equal)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `ordered`, `sort`, `ordering`
